<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Othée</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1408</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Othée was fought on 23 September 1408 near Othée, north-west of Liège. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-the-fearless">John the Fearless of Burgundy</a>, with his brother-in-law William, Count of Hainaut, crushed the citizens of Liège, who had rebelled against their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>-elect, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-duke-of-bavaria">John of Bavaria</a>. Thousands of Liègeois were killed, the city lost its charters, and the victory is often linked with John's nickname 'the Fearless'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-othee.jpg" alt="Battle of Othée" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eric Vyncke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monument_Bataille_oth%C3%A9e.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
